---
description: UI and UX rules for personal finance app
globs:
  - app/**/*.tsx
  - components/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: true
---

Design principles:

- Use clean spacing and strong hierarchy
- Use shadcn/ui patterns consistently
- Prefer card-based layout for dashboards
- Use tabs only when the content groups are clearly related
- Keep the primary user journey obvious
- Minimize cognitive load
- Make financial numbers easy to scan
- Use typography and spacing as the main visual structure

Layout rules:

- Desktop first for data-heavy dashboards, but fully responsive
- Mobile should collapse dashboards into meaningful stacked cards
- Sticky top summary bars are preferred for key metrics
- Keep page width controlled; avoid stretched content
- Use grid layouts for metric cards and dashboard modules
- Tables must support filtering, searching, sorting, and export

Number formatting:

- Always format money clearly
- Show currency symbol consistently
- Use positive/negative visual cues consistently
- Percentages should include comparison basis where relevant
- Large values should support compact notation only where appropriate
- Never truncate important financial figures ambiguously

Dashboard rules:

- Each page must have a summary section first
- Follow with trends
- Then breakdowns
- Then detailed tables / history
- Then AI insights / recommended actions

Charts:

- Avoid decorative charts
- Every chart must have an analytical purpose
- Prefer line charts for trends
- Prefer stacked bars for composition over time
- Prefer donut/pie only for high-level category distribution
- Always label time ranges clearly
- Provide comparison to previous period where useful

Transaction UX:

- Transactions should be easy to scan and edit
- Merchant, amount, category, and date must stand out
- Recurring, transfer, subscription, and anomaly states should be visible
- Editing a category should be frictionless
- Support bulk actions for categorization

Accessibility:

- Maintain strong contrast
- Avoid relying on color alone
- Support keyboard navigation
- Use semantic HTML
- Tooltips should explain financial terms when needed

Copywriting:

- Use plain English
- Avoid accounting jargon unless necessary
- Explain complex finance concepts in user-friendly language
- Write concise labels
- Empty states should guide the next action

The app should look like a premium finance workspace, not a startup demo.
